  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO- Kalinga Prize for the Popularisation of Science</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UNESCO Kalinga Prize for the Popularisation of Science is UNESCO&apos;s oldest prize, established in 1950. It is jointly funded by the Kalinga Foundation Trust, the Government of the State of Orissa (India), and the Government of India. The Prize is awarded biannually to reward the outstanding contribution of an individual, institution, other entity or non-governmental organization in writing, editing, lecturing, directing or producing multi-media programmes, which have enabled to help interpret science, research and technology to the public. A candidate may only be nominated by the UNESCO Member States or affiliated NGOs, no self nomination are considered.</narrative>
  </description>
